  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "120",
  "quote": "No landlord may increase the rent charged to a tenant, or to an assignee under section 95, during the term of their tenancy by more than the guideline, except in accordance with section 126 or 127 or an agreement under section 121 or 123.",
  "reason": "The clause is consistent with the Act's rules for rent increases, which permit a landlord to increase rent by up to the guideline amount (section 120) once every 12 months (section 119) with at least 90 days' written notice in a form approved by the Board (section 116). Because it does not conflict with the Act, it is not void under section 4."
}

